00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.710
the Ethereum and the Ethereum Classic Blockchain, right?

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.170
And this is clearly, ah, very bad, right.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:57.800
You don't want to face lia- liabilities for twice as many digital dollars as you've issued.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:01.900
So the moral of the story here is that mining is actually

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:05.895
pretty scary for digital asset issuers, right?

00:12:05.895 --> 00:12:08.095
I mean, first of all mining is anonymous, right?

00:12:08.095 --> 00:12:11.325
All it means is that somebody with sufficient resources has, you know,

00:12:11.325 --> 00:12:15.895
executed the computation to extend or or fork the history.

00:12:15.895 --> 00:12:17.850
And, you know, so far,

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:20.020
we've been kind of lucky with the high pr- profile.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.905
forks have been kind of announced in advance and

00:12:22.905 --> 00:12:26.425
each has been assigned a separate name like Ethereum and Ethereum Classic.

00:12:26.425 --> 00:12:28.610
But you can imagine, you know,

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:32.470
a branch where it's just like a fork with like two different, you know,

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.710
competing pools of miners were kind of duking it out and saying, hey,

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:39.190
everybody join our mining pool because then we'll give you uh, more rewards.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.350
And if this goes on for a while and they're both

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:43.510
playing under the same rules and the mining is anonymous,

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:45.110
you can't even name the two different forks.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.530
So how are you going to say like,

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:50.745
who's allowed to redeem your tokens that you've issued and who isn't.

00:12:50.745 --> 00:12:54.595
Another problem is that the mining rewards themselves might actually be- provide

00:12:54.595 --> 00:12:59.330
insufficient incentive for securing your transaction.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:03.815
So even on the biggest blockchains like Bitcoin and Ethereum,

00:13:03.815 --> 00:13:06.800
the mining rewards today are under $10 million a day,

