which is dwarfed by,

00:13:08.605 --> 00:13:10.360
you know the number of, you know,

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.490
the amount of sort of dollars,

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:14.040
like there's trillions of dollars moving between banks on a,

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.360
on a daily basis.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:22.260
Right. And what's kind of worse is that now there's like Bitcoin futures, you can trade.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.795
So If you're a miner and you're about to do something really weird,

00:13:24.795 --> 00:13:27.530
you can actually hedge yourself against the damage you're going to do to

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.850
Bitcoin by selling a bunch of Bitcoin futures, right?

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:33.215
And then you can kind of wreak all kinds of havoc.

00:13:33.215 --> 00:13:35.360
And the other thing is there might be non-financial kind

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:37.330
of extrinsic incentives to do this, right.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:39.090
Let's say you're a forward looking company and you say, hey,

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:42.430
I'm going to issue my stock on Bitcoin by using,

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:44.650
you know, colored coins to represent my shares

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:46.600
and now my stock can be traded in a Blockchain.

